      },
      "lineNbr": 427,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-19T00:50:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What are your thoughts on this approach versus something more radical to achieve our stated goals? \n\nOn the one hand, this approach wasn\u0027t much coding which is nice.  On the other, I worry we\u0027ll regret tying the DP module states to the AP driving VDMs.  It makes it convenient to let the module run ExitMode, but it also means that if we do something like support active DP cable entry, then the module and AP would need updated to stay in step with each other. \n\nAt any rate, I was debating about whether the HPD logic could be modularized better so we don\u0027t have to move the DP states along.  I\u0027m not totally certain about ExitMode... we could just maintain whatever SVID/SOP* combinations we\u0027ve sent EnterMode to somewhere and iterate on them generically.",
      "parentUuid": "1dda08f5_7059899f",
      "revId": "507a3f459996dfc59d4b1ed81161ca43761b0a68",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "437145e0_eebc2cf1",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 427,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-19T19:06:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Before too long, you\u0027ll need to add analogous logic for TBT, which already supports cables. To my mind, that\u0027s one argument against putting this here. If we need logic like this, it makes more sense in the mode modules.\n\nTo avoid having the modules keep up one way or another, I think you\u0027d need to do something generic like you described. If we had a mechanism to do this, I\u0027d want the AP to transmit callable objects to the EC after it enters a mode. The EC could then use that as a callback to exit the mode when the AP shuts down. But I don\u0027t think we have anything resembling that capability right now.\n\nUltimately, if you want the AP to support modes that the EC doesn\u0027t, you\u0027ll need something generic. But I\u0027d suggest that that should go in some kind of `generic_alt_mode.c` module, not the top-level DPM control flow.",
      "parentUuid": "1fd9f1d9_052e4319",
      "revId": "507a3f459996dfc59d4b1ed81161ca43761b0a68",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
